sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — MorphoEval overall 89.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py` (89.2/100; v2 91.3). The single open v2 item is closed: Section 1b (`nodal_signal`, `nodal_to_cortical_tension_target`, `cortical_tension_mismatch_gamma`, `integrate_nodal_cortical_tension_dynamics`, L229-L344) and Section 2b (`simulate_nodal_coupled_internalization`, `run_nodal_dose_sweep`, L773-L1030) couple a time-dependent marginal Nodal/TGF-beta field to per-cell cortical tensions that are relaxed every MCS and fed back into a per-cell-pair DITH lattice energy; the coupled model yields 5 mesendoderm / 2 endoderm tiers at shield stage, the Krieg hierarchy by 4.87 hpf, Delta_r = +0.350 at 7 hpf, and no sorting in the Nodal-null control, with three new Lean theorems (6 total, 0 sorrys). The re-score is nevertheless lower than v2 because the round exposed defects the v2 audit had not scored: the static regimes' lattice uses one homotypic bond energy for E-E and M-M contacts although `compute_dith_tensions` returns gamma_EE = 70 != gamma_MM = 150 (so the static energy is not Brodland's), the v2 dataset JSON carried heterotypic adhesion values inconsistent with its own gamma_het anchor (corrected here), two v2 measurement methods carried hard-coded \"p=0.0001\" strings (removed), the specimen is a whole-blastoderm transplant proxy rather than a germ-layer progenitor aggregate, and the Nodal row has no specimen or digitised gradient behind it; the 7 new DOIs were recorded offline. Overall 89.2/100 (faithfulness 88.3, reproducibility 91.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8beed34; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py at 8beed34, image/png, 695518 B, 3000×1890 px, artifact_sha256 5ffd7144ad26d4d8b06fe5b2d7ddf385312e2ed564432552abf59cecd5490808 (sha256 5ffd7144ad26d4d8b06fe5b2d7ddf385312e2ed564432552abf59cecd5490808), spec_fingerprint 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587; artifact_sha256: 5ffd7144ad26d4d8b06fe5b2d7ddf385312e2ed564432552abf59cecd5490808. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Brodland (2002) J. Biomech. Eng. Eqs. 1-4: Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) decomposing cell-cell interfacial tension into actomyosin cortical tension minus cadherin adhesion (gamma_{alpha,beta} = beta_alpha + beta_beta - omega_{alpha,beta}). | Krieg et al. (2008) Nature Cell Biology Figs. 1-4: AFM cortical tension hierarchy across zebrafish shield-stage germ-layer progenitors (beta_ectoderm ~ 50 < beta_mesoderm ~ 95 < beta_endoderm ~ 130 pN/um) obtained by lefty1 / cyclops / cyclops+casanova mRNA injection, concentric 3-germ-layer sorting, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition arrest, and caMLCK ectodermal cortical stiffening sorting reversal. | Maître et al. (2012) Science Eq. 1: Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle cos(theta) = 1 - gamma_cc/(2*gamma_cm) and normalized contact radius r_c/R = sin(theta). | Chen & Schier (2001), Dubrulle et al. (2015), van Boxtel et al. (2015), Hagos & Dougan (2007): Nodal (Squint/Cyclops) acts as a graded marginal morphogen whose signalling domain is set by a temporal window between sphere and shield stage and whose dose specifies mesoderm vs endoderm; Gritsman et al. (1999): MZoep embryos lack all mesendoderm.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D deformable DITH cell sorting across all 4 perturbation regimes (wild-type engulfment, caMLCK cortex reversal, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition, and high-HIT mushroom doublet) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446), a 7-point continuous beta_E sweep across the sorting inversion threshold beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um, and the Young-Dupré doublet contact curve. | Pass 3: a reduced time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling — 1D marginal Nodal field C(x,t) with range lambda = 3 tiers and rise time tau_N = 0.6 h from 4.0 hpf, two-threshold Hill dose -> cortical tension target (beta_E/beta_M/beta_N = 50/95/130 pN/um), first-order cortex relaxation tau_beta = 0.5 h, and a continuous-cortex DITH closure gamma_ij = (2/3)|beta_i - beta_j| re-evaluated every MCS inside the lattice sorter; the model reproduces 5 mesendoderm / 2 endoderm tiers at shield stage, establishes the Krieg hierarchy by 4.87 hpf, reaches Delta_r = +0.350 at 7 hpf, and gives Delta_r = 0 with no mesendoderm in the Nodal-null (C0 = 0) control; 5-point C0 dose sweep. | Computer-vision segmentation of a zebrafish blastoderm transplantation GFP/RFP micrograph (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`) across both layered engulfment (Row B, radial profile r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844) and the protruding mushroom doublet (Row C, empirical r_c/R = 0.9717).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice DITH representation of 3D zebrafish germ-layer progenitor reaggregates and blastoderm transplants; the circular 60-cell disc with medium all round is a reaggregate, not an embryo, so 'internalization' is sorting toward the disc centre. | The Nodal coupling is 1D in tier distance from the margin, each cell's Nodal exposure is frozen to its tier of origin (specification memory), there is no epiboly / YSL motion and no Lefty feedback; lambda, K_M, K_N, tau_N and tau_beta were chosen to reproduce recalled literature anchors (~5 mesendoderm tiers, endoderm from tiers 1-2), not fitted to a digitised pSmad2 profile. | The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia whole-blastoderm / yolk-cell transplant micrograph, not a Krieg et al. (2008) progenitor aggregate or a shield-stage internalization image; it is a proxy for layered GFP/RFP sorting, and no specimen underlies the Nodal row of the figure.; does_not_claim: Does not model sub-second single-molecule E-cadherin bond rupture kinetics, whole-embryo epiboly yolk-syncytial-layer microtubule pulling, 2D/3D Nodal-Lefty reaction-diffusion, or quantitative pSmad2 gradient fits.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py:1595-1702 — all sorting morphometrics are single-seed point values; add a seed ensemble (e.g. 8 seeds) with mean +/- s.d. for Delta_r, the hierarchy time and the tier counts, and sweep lambda / tau_beta / kappa (CLI-only at L1825-L1827) in a panel so the Nodal parameters are tested, not only exposed.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py:496-508 and 668-680 — the static regimes and the 3-layer sorter use a single homotypic bond energy j_hom = 4.0 for E-E and M-M (and N-N) contacts although `compute_dith_tensions` (L136-L184) returns gamma_EE = 70 != gamma_MM = 150; with those values Brodland's own sorting inequality gamma_EM > (gamma_EE + gamma_MM)/2 fails (30 < 110), so the static lattice energy is a Steinberg J-matrix, not the DITH energy. Adopt the continuous-cortex closure of `_cell_pair_J` (L840-L847) in the static regimes too, or carry measured gamma_hom values, and re-test regimes I-IV.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py:826 and 892-896 — Nodal exposure is frozen to the tier of origin and the field is 1D in tier distance (`nodal_signal`, L232-L253); after a cell moves its C(x,t) is never re-evaluated and there is no Lefty feedback or epiboly. Implement a 2D Nodal/Lefty reaction-diffusion field on the lattice (re-evaluated at the cell's current position) and vendor a digitised pSmad2 profile (Dubrulle et al. 2015) so lambda, K_M and K_N are fitted rather than chosen to reproduce the recalled anchors at L1666-L1680.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_reference.json:6-74 and paper_citations.bib:57-131 — the 7 Pass 3 DOIs (Chen & Schier 2001, Dubrulle 2015, van Boxtel 2015, Hagos & Dougan 2007, Gritsman 1999, Warga & Nüsslein-Volhard 1999, Kimmel 1995) were recorded offline and are flagged `doi_verification: not resolved`; resolve them against the registry and pin figure/table numbers for the 50/95/130 pN/um AFM values.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_reference.json:75-88 and 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py:1405-1510 — the only specimen is a whole-blastoderm / yolk-cell transplant micrograph, and Row C (Nodal coupling) has no specimen at all. Vendor a CC-BY shield-stage internalization or pSmad2 gradient micrograph (or Krieg 2008 Fig. 2-type aggregate image if licensable) and add a C-row specimen panel with a quantitative comparison." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.892"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

